# the sticks for m48_joyown.keys (the format is m48_joy.joy's), for a play
# on the port's own clock: every move and press is a tap of 0.056 s, a
# little more than the 0.0549 s between two of the timer routine's reads
# of the sticks, so each is read once or twice whenever it falls and a
# side's part takes it once (as the keys' taps of 0.06 s in make_two.py).
# The first stick is there from the program's start
0 0,570,570,0
# the first stick: left, right, up, down, right and down at once
26.000 0,100,570,0
26.056 0,570,570,0
27.000 0,1100,570,0
27.056 0,570,570,0
28.000 0,570,100,0
28.056 0,570,570,0
29.000 0,570,1100,0
29.056 0,570,570,0
30.000 0,1100,1100,0
30.056 0,570,570,0
# the second stick, there when F6 looks for it at 32 and 33
31.000 1,600,500,0
# its left, right, up, down
35.000 1,100,500,0
35.056 1,600,500,0
36.000 1,1100,500,0
36.056 1,600,500,0
37.000 1,600,100,0
37.056 1,600,500,0
38.000 1,600,1000,0
38.056 1,600,500,0
# both at once
39.000 0,100,570,0
39.000 1,1100,500,0
39.056 0,570,570,0
39.056 1,600,500,0
# the first side's stick not wanted from 40: nothing
41.000 0,100,570,0
41.056 0,570,570,0
# wanted again from 42
43.500 0,100,570,0
43.556 0,570,570,0
# each side's button
45.000 0,570,570,1
45.056 0,570,570,0
46.000 1,600,500,1
46.056 1,600,500,0
